      "severity": "medium",
      "confidence": "high",
      "location": {
        "page": 1,
        "page_label": "1",
        "section": "Abstract",
        "text_quote": "the same rate as between two human coders",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "On the pilot, the LLM agrees with a human coder on the relevance of 97 percent of the articles, the same rate as between two human coders.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Tables 3 and 4 do give 33 of 34 (97%) for both pairs. Section 4 says 'the sample is too small to test whether the two agreement rates differ. The results are thus indicative only.' Only 3 of the 34 articles are coded relevant by the pilot coder, so 30 of the 33 agreements are agreements on not-relevant articles. Section 8 repeats that the comparison cannot be tested. The abstract gives no hint of these limits. The introduction describes the rates as 'very close' and also omits the caveat.",
