      "claim_text": "Applied to 3,187 articles, the pipeline finds 92 articles reporting an opening, which we group into 43 projects across 14 of 15 counties, 29 of them dated to the day or month.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "Validation (Section 4) covers only the 34-article pilot. Section 8 says 'a random sample from the full run of 3,187 articles should also be checked against human coding.' In the pilot, the LLM's majority vote flagged 4 articles as relevant and the pilot coder agreed on 3 (Table 4). The pilot yield of true openings among keyword hits was also low. The precision of the 92 articles and the accuracy of the 43 grouped projects and their dates are therefore unmeasured. Section 8 also says project grouping was done by hand in this paper. The abstract and conclusion present the counts as results without these qualifications.",
